description:
Department/ Unit: Faculty of Social Science
Closing Date: Until the post is filled
The Gender Studies Programme at The Chinese University of Hong Kong is the ﬁrst programme in gender studies in the tertiary education sector in Hong Kong. It is an interdisciplinary unit based in the Faculty of Social Science, oﬀering Bachelor, MA, MPhil and PhD programmes. The forward-looking team of Gender Studies Programme is inviting applications for the post of Assistant Professor on substantiation (tenure) track to join from the academic year 2026-27 or as soon as possible.
The appointee is expected to
(a) conduct research and secure research grants;
(b) teach courses at undergraduate and postgraduate levels;
(c) supervise students’ theses; and
(d) undertake administrative duties.
Applicants should possess:
(i) a PhD degree by the time of reporting for duty;
(ii) relevant research experience in gender/sex/sexuality-related areas;
(iii) demonstrated potential/ ability for high quality research; and
(iv) a strong sense of responsibility and commitment to excellent research, teaching, and service.
Applicants specializing in any of the following areas are preferred:
• Empirical gender/sex/sexuality studies
• ⁠Human and social development
• Social sustainability or sustainable development
Applicants who specialize in a subject field in Social Science (e.g., Journalism, Social Work, Political Science, Economics) that adds to the diversity of the existing team or whose profile strengthens the programme’s internationalization are preferred. Applicants in cognate subjects (e.g., Education) will also be considered if they possess a profile of a good match to Social Science and especially if they are strong in quantitative empirical research.
Application Procedure
Candidates should complete and submit the online application form with the following documents/information:
(a) latest CV;
(b) a cover letter;
(c) a research statement;
(d) two sample publications;
(e) a teaching statement;
(f) copies of academic credentials and relevant certificates;
(g) names and contact information of three referees; and
(h) evidence of teaching performance, if applicable.
Appointment will initially be made on contract basis for up to three years, renewable subject to mutual agreement, and may lead to a longer-term appointment or substantiation.
Review of applications will start in April 2026 and continue until the post is filled.
For more information about the programme, please visit: https://www.gender.cuhk.edu.hk/ . For initial enquiries, please contact Ms. Winnie Ling of the programme (email: winnieling@cuhk.edu.hk ).
The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk .

Department/ Unit: Department of Physics
Closing Date: Until the post(s) is/ are filled
Post(s) Specification:
The Department of Physics invites applications for tenure-track or tenured faculty positions (at all ranks) from the academic year 2026-27.
Outstanding candidates working in the areas of physics and materials science currently being pursued in the Department, are welcome to apply, including:
- Astrophysics and Cosmology;
- Atomic, Molecular, and Optical Physics;
- Biophysics and Soft Matter Physics;
- Complex Systems and Fluids;
- Condensed Matter Physics;
- Materials Science;
- Quantum Information Science and Technology;
- Particle Physics; and
- Quantum Information Science and Technology.
Applicants should (i) have a relevant PhD degree with postdoctoral research experience; (ii) demonstrate a track record of research accomplishments, potential for establishing a significant externally funded research programme; and (iii) have a strong interest in teaching at undergraduate and postgraduate levels.
Appointment(s) will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment(s) or substantiation.
Application Procedure
Applicants should submit an online application and attach a full resume, research plan, teaching statement, copies of academic credentials, a publication list and/ or abstracts of selected published papers (if any), together with names, addresses and fax numbers/ e-mail addresses of three referees to whom the applicants' consent has been given for their providing references (unless otherwise specified).
Applications will be accepted until the positions are filled.
The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post(s) above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk .

Department of Social Work
Professor
(Ref. 240002SJ) Closing date: Until the post is filled
As a world-leading centre of social work education and research, the Department is dedicated to developing and disseminating scientific rigorous and socially impactful social work knowledge for human betterment and social development, such as in the niche areas on aging, mental health, family, and social policy. We aspire, through our research and evaluation work, to improve the lives of vulnerable and disadvantaged groups, deepen our understanding of social issues and promote evidence-based practice locally and globally. The Department is looking for candidates who embrace these goals and values.
The Department is seeking a well-established scholar who will contribute to the continuous development and enhancement of the Department in social work research and education. More specifically, our ideal candidate is expected to:
Have a clear vision of and be dedicated to quality social work research, education and professional training ;
Have a strong record of scientific research and publications in social work or social administration;
Be experienced in capacity building in an academic department of social work;
Be committed to nurturing and mentoring future thought leaders in the department, discipline and profession;
Possess transformational leadership and excellent communication skills;
Be enthusiastic and experienced in fostering transdisciplinary, cross-disciplinary, and international collaborations; and
Understand Hong Kong, China, and Asian culture and initiate dialogues among different cultures
The Department and the University are committed to attracting top talent and offer competitive salary and benefit packages commensurate with qualifications and experience. Outstanding candidates may be specially considered for substantive appointment forthwith.
Application Procedure
The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk.

Department/ Unit: The Nethersole School of Nursing
Closing Date: Until the post is filled
The Nethersole School of Nursing, formerly the Department of Nursing, was established in the Faculty of Medicine in 1991. The School is committed to excellence in teaching, research and in the promotion of the highest standards of nursing practice. Further information about the School is available at http://www.nur.cuhk.edu.hk/ .
Assistant Professor
Applicants should have (i) a PhD degree in nursing or a related discipline; (ii) experience in tertiary-level research and teaching; and (iii) a research record demonstrated by publishing papers in refereed journals. Substantial publications in international journals and a record of award of competitive research grants will be advantageous.
Research Assistant Professor
Applicants should have (i) a PhD degree in nursing or a related discipline; (ii) strong academic credentials and outstanding academic records; (iii) firm commitment in good quality teaching and research; and (iv) a research record demonstrated by publishing papers in high-impact refereed journals. Applicants with collaborative research projects involving different disciplines will have an advantage.
The appointee will be expected to (a) apply for external competitive research grants; (b) develop and participate in collaborative research projects; (c) supervise postgraduate students; (d) teach courses at undergraduate and/or postgraduate levels; (e) take up research administrative duties of the School; and (f) perform other duties as assigned by the Director or his delegates.
Applicants should complete the on-line application form and upload the followings:
1. full resume;
2. copies of academic credentials;
3. full publication list, with web link of the papers;
4. three recent publication samples;
5. a statement of research interest;
6. citations (Google or ISI);
7. an indication, in %, the share of contributions among authors of a publication;
8. evidence of teaching performance, if any; and
9. names and e-mails addresses of three referees to whom the applicant's consent has been given for providing reference (unless otherwise specified).
Appointment of Assistant Professor will normally be made on contract basis for two years initially commencing as soon as possible, which, subject to performance and mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation later.
Appointment of Research Assistant Professor will initially be made on contract basis for up to two years commencing as soon as possible, renewable subject to good performance, funding availability and mutual agreement.
The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk .

INTERNATIONAL OFFICE
Reshaping tomorrow’s global leaders is one of the International Office’s top priorities on the internationalisation agenda. Partnership has taken on new meanings in today’s fast-changing world. The Office works closely with its partners worldwide and the university community to bring innovative and impactful collaborations for tomorrow’s world. It conducts proactive global outreach for branding and partnerships. Innovativeness has been at the core of its success.
The Office is dedicated to nurturing global inclusive generations. It seeks to create a diverse, inclusive and engaged community by offering a truly global education. It connects the university community with world-renowned academics and experts, industry players, as well as senior government officials, by hosting various intellectually stimulating programmes and initiatives (https://intl.hkbu.edu.hk).
Assistant Director (25260540)
The University seeks a high-calibre and experienced leader to advance its global education and cultivate meaningful global partnerships. This role plays a pivotal part in shaping and advancing strategy, leading complex cross-unit programmes, and delivering high-impact initiatives that enhance student learning and institutional reputation.
Reporting to the Director of the International Office, the ideal candidate will bring well-rounded knowledge and skill sets to drive strategic planning, policy alignment, and the end-to-end execution of major global initiatives, achieving core institutional-level objectives.
Responsibilities:
Support the Director of INTL in overseeing all functions, with a primary focus on Global Partnerships and Education;
Provide strategic leadership in the planning, implementation, and continuous enhancement of global education initiatives, ensuring impactful and best student learning experiences;
Drive the execution of the University’s internationalisation strategy, aligning global initiatives with institutional priorities and evolving global higher education trends;
Monitor and analyse global developments in higher education to inform strategic decision-making and the design of innovative educational initiatives and partnerships;
Identify, assess, and develop new international markets and partnership opportunities to expand the University’s global presence and reputation;
Build and maintain strong relationships with senior leaders of key global stakeholders;
Promote a diverse and inclusive campus culture, and develop initiatives to support intercultural awareness and integration among students;
Represent the University at international conferences, forums, and high-level engagements to enhance institutional visibility and influence;
Oversee the development and delivery of international marketing and communication strategies.
Lead a professional team, fostering a high-performance culture, leadership capability, and cross-cultural competence; and
Prepare high-level reports, proposals and presentations for senior management and external stakeholders.
Requirements:
A recognised university degree, with a minimum of 10 years of relevant professional and managerial experience;
Outstanding command of written and spoken English and Chinese;
Strong strategic thinking, analytical capability, and presentation skills;
Demonstrated ability to lead complex projects and deliver results in a fast-paced, dynamic environment;
Sound judgement, intellectual curiosity, and a track record of innovation and problem-solving;
High cultural intelligence, with a strong commitment to diversity and inclusion;
A solid understanding of the global higher education landscape is a definite advantage; and
Strong communication and interpersonal skills.
Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and give a presentation.
The initial appointment will be offered on a fixed-term contract of three years. Re-appointment thereafter will be subject to mutual agreement.
Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.
Application Procedure:
Applicants are invited to submit their applications at the HKBU e-Recruitment System. Those who are not invited for interview 4 months after submission of application may consider their applications unsuccessful. Details of the University’s Personal Information Collection Statement can be found at https://hro.hkbu.edu.hk/en/worklife-at-hkbu/employee-favourable-environment.html#privacy-policy.
The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, and the appointment will be made according to the terms and conditions applicable at the time of offer.
Review of applications will begin immediately until the position is filled.

SCHOOL OF CHINESE MEDICINE
CENTRE FOR CHINESE HERBAL MEDICINE DRUG DEVELOPMENT
Postdoctoral Research Fellow / Senior Research Assistant in clinical research (25260249)
The applicant is expected to manage clinical study in the areas of Chinese medicine, biomedical sciences or related disciplines.
Responsibilities:
Responsible for planning and leading the delivery of all components of a clinical study to time, cost, and quality from protocol development, study start-up through closeout activities and clinical study report;
Clinical study subject recruitment and data monitoring;
Leading and managing multi-functional project team;
Being the primary point of contact for the assigned project; and
Undertake any other duties assigned.
Requirements:
A Ph.D. or postgraduate degree with at least 5 years of clinical research, or at least 2 years recent clinical research experience in the capacity of project manager/equivalent (clinical study team lead, clinical study manager, etc.);
Holding or qualifying to apply for a Chinese Medicine Practices license;
Experience managing randomised controlled trials in therapeutic research for Gastrointestinal diseases is preferred;
Experience with ICH-GCP guidelines and understandings on pharmaceutical product development is an advantage;
Should have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese, as well as good interpersonal and organisational skills;
Should be responsible, attentive to details and able to work independently; and
Innovative, self-motivated with good planning and organisational skills are essential.
Those with less experience or lower qualifications may be considered for the post of Senior Research Assistant.
The initial appointment will be offered on a fixed-term contract of 1 year. Re-appointment thereafter will be subject to performance and availability of funding.
A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.
Application Procedure:
Applicants are invited to submit their applications at the HKBU e-Recruitment System. Those who are not invited for interview 8 weeks after submission of application may consider their applications unsuccessful. Details of the University's Personal Information Collection Statement can be found at https://hro.hkbu.edu.hk/en/worklife-at-hkbu/employee-favourable-environment.html#privacy-policy.
The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, and the appointment will be made according to the terms and conditions applicable at the time of offer.
Review of applications is ongoing until the positions are filled.

OFFICE OF INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY
Senior Information Technology Officer (Customer Services/User Support) [Role: End User Computing] (25260678)
Position Description
Reporting to the Senior Information Technology Manager (Customer Services/User Support) of Office of Information Technology, the appointee will provide the first line of support to the University community in the use of IT services for the purpose of teaching and learning as well as a business operation.
Responsibilities:
Provide IT support and delivery effective solution for the IT user services;
Deliver technical support and problem solving to VIP users;
Participate in digital workplace projects, including system upgrade, new services rollout, and software refreshment;
Assist patch management and computer standard imaging rollout to ensure security compliance and adherence to standard operating procedures;
Maintain printing management system to ensure reliable printing services;
Technical proficiency across Windows 11, Microsoft 365, macOS, and mobile platforms (iOS/Android);
Investigate and analyse technical problems escalated from the IT Service Desk;
Collaborate with IT team, users, external vendors to manage the assigned IT projects; and
Perform ad hoc assignments and responsibilities requested by supervisor.
Requirements:
A bachelor’s degree in information technology, computer science or related discipline;
Minimum 4 years or above of relevant work experience;
Hands on experience in supporting Windows/MacOS, Microsoft 365, PC hardware and printing management system;
Excellent problem-solving skills with a technology-driven and analytical mindset;
Good written and verbal communication skills with the ability to work under pressure; and
Independent, self-motivated, quick learner, good team player, a strong sense of responsibility and able to work under pressure.
Shortlisted candidates will be invited to sit for a written test.
The initial appointment will be made on a fixed-term contract of two years. Re-appointment thereafter is subject to performance review, mutual agreement and availability of funding.
Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.
Application Procedure:
Applicants are invited to submit their applications at the HKBU e-Recruitment System. Those who are not invited for interview 8 weeks after submission of application may consider their applications unsuccessful. Details of the University’s Personal Information Collection Statement can be found at https://hro.hkbu.edu.hk/en/worklife-at-hkbu/employee-favourable-environment.html#privacy-policy .
The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, and the appointment will be made according to the terms and conditions applicable at the time of offer.
Review of applications is ongoing until the position is filled.

SCHOOL OF CONTINUING EDUCATION
The School of Continuing Education, one of the seven Faculties/Schools of the University and a major provider of continuing and professional education in Hong Kong, offers a wide range of full-time and part-time programmes at the post-secondary, undergraduate and postgraduate levels for young learners and working adults. It also offers in-house training and short courses to meet the community needs and market demands. Operated on a self-financed basis, the School and its College of International Education currently employ about 400 full-time staff and 550 part-time instructors. The School is inviting applications for the following position:
Accounting Manager (Income and Project) (25260561)
The School aims to complete registration as a post-secondary college within the next few years, committed to enhancing the internationalisation and diversification of higher education, and developing distinctive and professional programmes that address the manpower needs of society. Once this strategic development is solidified, it is planned that the role will evolve with a long-term prospect.
To support this transformation, the Accounts and Purchasing Section is seeking an Accounting Manager to support the Senior Accounting Manager to oversee various functions of the Section to enable the School’s strategic goals.
Responsibilities:
Oversee daily accounting transactions, including purchasing, budget checking, income collection, payment;
Assist in managing procurement activities including supplier and tender management;
Maintain accurate financial records by ensuring all income and expenditures are properly recorded, implementing controls to prevent errors such as double payments, and handling payment processing for purchases;
Collaborate with internal divisions of the School and the Finance Office of the University to resolve accounting and purchasing matters;
Supervise and guide subordinate staff to support efficient operations;
Coordinate programme-related tasks such as handling enquiries and liaise with administrators;
Conduct analytical reviews of financial statements and budgets;
Lead inventory control and financial administration;
Assist in the annual budgeting cycle; and
Perform ad hoc duties as assigned.
Requirements:
A bachelor’s degree in accounting or finance, with membership in a recognised professional accounting body;
Minimum of 5 years of relevant experience, preferably in higher education or public sector settings;
Strong analytical and reporting skills; proficiency in Advanced Excel and common accounting systems;
Sound understanding of internal controls, compliance and funding code application;
Proven supervisory experience with a track record of effective, deadline-driven teams;
Very good command of written and spoken English and Chinese;
High competency in computer applications and compilation of statistical data;
Well-organised, detail-minded, highly self-motivated, and the ability to work independently under minimal supervision; and
Strong communication and problem-solving skills.
Shortlisted candidates will be invited to sit for a written test.
The initial appointment will be offered on a fixed-term contract ending in August 2027. Re-appointment thereafter is subject to mutual agreement and availability of funding.
Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.
Application Procedure:
Applicants are invited to submit their applications at the HKBU e-Recruitment System. Those who are not invited for interview 8 weeks after submission of applications may consider their applications unsuccessful. Details of the University’s Personal Information Collection Statement can be found at https://hro.hkbu.edu.hk/en/worklife-at-hkbu/employee-favourable-environment.html#privacy-policy.
The School reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, and the appointment will be made according to the terms and conditions applicable at the time of offer.
Review of applications is ongoing until the position is filled.

OFFICE OF INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY
Senior IT Manager (Student Information System Modernisation and Cloud Migration) (26270012)
Position description
Reporting to the Assistant Director of the Application and Integration Services Section, the Senior Information Technology Manager serves as both a strategic leader and subject matter expert in the modernisation of Student Information System (SIS) and the migration of IT applications to cloud. This pivotal role is responsible for leading a team of internal and external vendors to deliver the modernisation and cloud migration initiatives.
Responsibilities:
Lead and oversee strategic initiatives focused on modernising SIS and migrating IT applications to cloud;
Champion continuous service improvement and innovation in line with the institution’s objectives;
Collaborate with cross-functional teams to deliver integrated, user-centered solutions that enhance stakeholder satisfaction;
Provide expert guidance on application / system architecture, modernisation strategies, cloud migration, and emerging technology trends;
Manage project planning, execution, and governance to ensure effective and timely delivery of initiatives;
Act as the subject matter expert, supervising internal teams and external consultants from system integrators;
Engage with business users to gather requirements and translate them into actionable user stories for application development and enhancement;
Work closely with Infrastructure and Security teams to facilitate smooth project execution;
Identify, assess, and manage vendors and consultants, including contract negotiation and compliance oversight;
Monitor and analyse system performance metrics to identify opportunities for optimisation and improvement; and
Perform ad hoc assignments and responsibilities requested by supervisor.
Requirements:
A bachelor’s degree in information technology, computer science, or a related discipline;
At least 10 years of experience in IT application modernisation and cloud migration;
Professional certification in public cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure, GCP, Alibaba Cloud) is an advantage;
Solid experience with relational database management systems such as Sybase or Microsoft SQL Server;
Demonstrated team leadership, including managing cross-functional teams and both internal and external resources;
Strong project management and stakeholder engagement skills; PMP certification is an advantage;
Comprehensive knowledge of IT applications relevant to tertiary education and university environments is desirable;
Proven ability to translate strategic vision into practical plans and measurable outcomes;
Exceptional analytical and problem-solving abilities, with a talent for converting business requirements into technical solutions; and
Outstanding communication and interpersonal skills, enabling effective collaboration with stakeholders at all levels.
Shortlisted candidates will be invited to sit for a written test.
The initial appointment will be offered on a fixed-term contract of two and a half years.
Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.
Application Procedure:
Applicants are invited to submit their applications at the HKBU e-Recruitment System. Those who are not invited for an interview 8 weeks after submission of their applications may consider their applications unsuccessful. Details of the University’s Personal Information Collection Statement can be found at https://hro.hkbu.edu.hk/en/worklife-at-hkbu/employee-favourable-environment.html#privacy-policy.
The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, and the appointment will be made according to the terms and conditions applicable at the time of offer.
Review of applications is ongoing until the position is filled.

ESTATES OFFICE
ADMINISTRATION AND ACCOUNTING SECTION
Senior Manager (Administration and Accounting) (25260299)
As the Section Head of the Administration and Accounting Section of the Estates Office, the Senior Manager will lead a team of administrative and accounting staff to:
Responsibilities:
Oversee the operation of the Estates Office at administrative level including:
Providing administrative management and support for the Estates Office;
Exploring initiatives and manage the development of smart systems to revamp the Estates Office’s administrative protocols in order to enhance efficiency and workflows;
Assisting in the review, formulation and implementation of works related, and carry out regular internal audits to ensure compliance with the policies and procedures of the University;
Managing the enquiry service for the University community and external parties;
Coordinating tasks associated with campus planning/development and facilities management, including organising consultation or workshops, etc. with both the University community and external stakeholders;
Providing secretarial service for committee and office meetings;
Prepare budget and monitor expenditures managed by the Estates Office, including:
Preparing, monitoring and reporting of budgets/expenditures managed by the Estates Office;
Managing and overseeing the staff and departmental costs;
Working closely with the project team and the Finance Office in the compilation and administration of the Lists of Consultants and the Lists of Tenderers of Works;
Take charge of recruitment/staffing matters, and resources management, including:
Manage and compile the Annual Performance Review exercise within the Estates Office and bridge with the Human Resources Office in all personnel and recruitment matters;
Keep and update the University’s space inventory regularly; and
Perform any other ad hoc duties as assigned.
Requirements:
A recognised bachelor’s degree in accounting, quantity surveying or a related discipline;
A qualified accountant and HKICPA member/finalist; or a full member of The Hong Kong Institute of Surveyors or the Royal Institution of Chartered Surveyors (Quantity Surveying discipline preferred;
At least 10 years of work experience in administrative management. Management of systems development or digital transformation, working in the construction field or familiarisation with Excel VBA will be advantages for consideration;
Excellent communication and language skills in both written and spoken English and Chinese;
Eagerness to learn and develop, and receptiveness to innovative technologies; and
Strong team player with can-do attitude, result-oriented mindset and positive energy.
The initial appointment will be offered on a fixed-term contract of two years. Re-appointment thereafter will be subject to performance review, mutual agreement and availability of funding.
Shortlisted candidates are required to sit for a written test.
Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.
Application Procedure:
Applicants are invited to submit their applications at the HKBU e-Recruitment System. Those who are not invited for interview 8 weeks after submission of application may consider their applications unsuccessful. Details of the University’s Personal Information Collection Statement can be found at https://hro.hkbu.edu.hk/en/worklife-at-hkbu/employee-favourable-environment.html#privacy-policy.
The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, and the appointment will be made according to the terms and conditions applicable at the time of offer.
Review of applications is ongoing until the position is filled.

OFFICE OF INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY
Information Technology Manager (Data Analytics) (25260274)
Reporting to the Senior Information Technology Manager, the appointee will be an in-house expert in advanced analytical and reporting output that is easy to understand for management decisions. The appointee should understand both the short-term and long-term strategy of the office and the University so as to put forward recommendations on how to leverage data analytics.
Responsibilities:
Responsible for guiding the design of data plan, working closely with a range of stakeholders including the rest of the architecture team, business users (both academic and administrative), and data providers;
Develop data quality standards and data quality control plans, conduct data quality management, tracking and monitoring, and establish data quality evaluation systems;
Develop advanced analytics, with AI and machine learning capability, to streamline existing data management process and improve efficiency;
Build predictive models to address problems and inform business decisions;
Manage and supervise third-party vendors and consultants for efficient and quality deliverables of different data analytics projects;
Perform ad hoc analysis on large/diverse datasets by using various tools and techniques using data-driven approach to measure and drive the success of initiatives, perform analyses with actionable insights; and
Perform other IT projects and assignments as assigned.
Requirements:
A bachelor’s degree in information technology, computer science or related discipline;
At least 7 years’ work experience in industry experience in Data Management & Analytics, with experience in a similar role as a Solution Architect or Data Architect is preferred;
Demonstrated track record in successfully implementing solutions in modern data architecture, Big Data, and/or traditional BI/DW/ETL encompassing both process and data analytics;
Solid experience of using Oracle Cloud, MS Azure, AWS, PowerBI, Tableau, QlikSense and/or statistical package such as SAS, Alteryx;
Knowledge of PL/SQL, Java, Stored Procedures, and Linux/Unix shell;
Ability to translate business needs into formal designs, and strong organisational, supervisory, and interpersonal skills needed to work effectively with a wide variety of internal and external resources; and
Possess excellent written and verbal communication skills to both technical and non-technical audiences, strong leadership skills and commitment-to-task.
Shortlisted candidates will be invited to sit for a written test.
The initial appointment will be offered on a fixed-term contract for up to two years. Re-appointment thereafter will be subject to mutual agreement.
Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.
Application Procedure:
Applicants are invited to submit their applications at the HKBU e-Recruitment System. Those who are not invited for an interview 8 weeks after submission of application may consider their applications unsuccessful. Details of the University’s Personal Information Collection Statement can be found at https://hro.hkbu.edu.hk/en/worklife-at-hkbu/employee-favourable-environment.html#privacy-policy.
The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, and the appointment will be made according to the terms and conditions applicable at the time of offer.
Review of applications is ongoing until the position is filled.

OFFICE OF INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY
Senior Systems Analyst (Special Project) (26270153)
We are seeking a highly skilled and experienced Senior Systems Analyst to join our dynamic team. As a Senior Systems Analyst, you will play a pivotal role in examining and analysing existing IT systems and business models and developing innovative solutions. Your expertise in software development lifecycles and your ability to translate client requirements into highly specified project briefs will be critical in driving successful project outcomes.
Responsibilities:
Map and document interfaces between legacy and new systems, ensuring seamless integration and efficient data transfer;
Demonstrate a thorough understanding of software development lifecycles, including requirements gathering, design, development, testing, implementation, and maintenance;
Collaborate with clients to translate their requirements into highly specified project briefs, ensuring clear communication and alignment of objectives;
Develop innovative solutions and undertake product development, leveraging your technical expertise and industry best practices;
Create and maintain comprehensive testing schedules for complete systems, ensuring rigorous quality assurance and adherence to project timelines;
Provide expert support to users on change control and system updates, ensuring minimal disruption to operations;
Deliver comprehensive training programs and user manuals for users of new systems, facilitating smooth adoption and maximising system utilisation; and
Perform other IT projects and assignments as assigned.
Requirements:
A bachelor’s degree in computer science, information technology, or a related field;
Minimum of 5 years of experience in system development and integration;
Advantageous to possess hands-on solid proven experience in at least two of the following development languages/tools: PHP, Java, NodeJS, SQL, MS Power Platform, and ETL tools;
Proven experience as a Systems Analyst, with a focus on software development;
Strong knowledge of software development lifecycles and methodologies;
Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to identify and address complex system issues;
Strong communication skills, with the ability to effectively collaborate with cross-functional teams and stakeholders; and
Certification in relevant areas such as ITIL or Agile methodologies is a plus.
Shortlisted candidates will be invited to sit for a written test.
The initial appointment will be offered on a fixed-term contract for up to two years. Re-appointment thereafter will be subject to performance review, mutual agreement and availability of funding.
Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.
Application Procedure:
Applicants are invited to submit their applications at the HKBU e-Recruitment System. Those who are not invited for an interview 8 weeks after submission of application may consider their applications unsuccessful. Details of the University’s Personal Information Collection Statement can be found at https://hro.hkbu.edu.hk/en/worklife-at-hkbu/employee-favourable-environment.html#privacy-policy.
The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, and the appointment will be made according to the terms and conditions applicable at the time of offer.
Review of applications is ongoing until the position is filled.

FACULTY OF ARTS & SOCIAL SCIENCES
ACADEMY OF GEOGRAPHY, SOCIOLOGY AND INTERNATIONAL STUDIES
Research Assistant (26270129)
The Academy of Geography, Sociology and International Studies, would like to invite applications for a Research Assistant with a strong interest in family demography, population ageing, and quantitative research using longitudinal panel data.
Responsibilities:
Work with the Principal Investigator on research projects related to intergenerational support, family relationships, and population ageing;
Assist with the harmonisation, management, and analysis of large-scale longitudinal ageing surveys, particularly the Health and Retirement Study (HRS) in the United States and the Survey of Health, Ageing and Retirement in Europe (SHARE);
Conduct data cleaning, variable construction, consistency checks, and documentation related to data harmonisation;
Assist with statistical analyses and the preparation of tables, figures, and other research outputs; and
Conduct literature reviews on relevant research topics.
Requirements:
A master’s degree in Sociology, Demography, Statistics, Data Science, Social Policy, Public Health, Economics, or a related discipline;
Strong quantitative research and data management skills;
Proficiency in Stata and/or R (preferably Stata);
Experience working with longitudinal/panel datasets;
Experience with large-scale ageing surveys would be an advantage;
Strong analytical, organisational, and communication skills; and
Good command of written and spoken English.
